<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>7.2.5: Practice</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m01765</md:content-id>
    <md:title>7.2.5: Practice</md:title>
    <md:uuid>35d50e3c-816e-4335-8754-eab477955059</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
    <section class="practice" id="sect-00001">
      <para id="para-00001">Complete the following questions to practice the skills you have learned in this lesson.</para>
      <exercise id="d58381a9-a116-4e2c-81b3-94b5b3cd37d1" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00001">
          <para id="para-00002">Pattern A</para>
          <para id="para-00003">Here are two patterns of dots.</para>
          <para id="para-00004">
                  <media alt="Four figures, labeled step 0 through 3. Step 0, no dots. Step 1, row of 4 dots. Step 2, 2 rows of 4 dots each. Step 3, 3 rows of 4 dots each.">
                <image mime-type="image/svg+xml" src="../../media/Algebra-1_08_04_10_01.svg"/>
              </media>
            
         </para>
          <para id="para-00005">Pattern B</para>
          <para id="para-00006">
                  <media alt="Four figures, step 0 through 3. Step 0, 2 dots. Step 1 row of 1 dot above a row of 2 dots. Step 2, 2 rows of 2 dots each, above a row of 2 dots. Step 3, 3 rows of 3 dots each, above row of 2 dots.">
                <image mime-type="image/jpeg" src="../../media/Algebra-1_08_04_10_02.jpg"/>
              </media>
            
         </para>
          <para id="para-00007">How many dots will there be in Step 4 of Pattern A?</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00001">
          <para id="para-00008">Correct! There will be 4 rows and 4 columns in Step 4.</para>
          <para id="para-00009">Try again. Revisit activity 7.2.2.</para>
          <para id="para-00010">The correct answer is 16.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="bedc6d9a-4d0e-4890-901f-10b2428b8966" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00002">
          <para id="para-00011">How many dots will there be in Step 4 of Pattern B?</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00002">
          <para id="para-00012">Correct! The relationship is <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:msup><m:mi>n</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
          <para id="para-00013">Try again. Revisit activity 7.2.2.</para>
          <para id="para-00014">The correct answer is 18.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="_78ee8dd0-f16f-48fb-9102-636e1d540108" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00003">
          <para id="para-00015">Which pattern shows a quadratic relationship between the step number and the number of dots?</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00003">
          <para id="para-00016">Correct! The relationship is <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:msup><m:mi>n</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
          <para id="para-00017">Try again. Revisit activities 7.2.3 and 7.2.4.</para>
          <para id="para-00018">The correct answer is Pattern B. This is because the relationship is <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:msup><m:mi>n</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="_5df82e90-55ae-44d5-ad83-882333ba247f" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00004">
          <para id="para-00019">Select two expressions that represent a quadratic relationship between the step number and the total number of dots. (If you get stuck, consider sketching the first few steps of each pattern as described by the expression.)</para>
          <para id="para-00020">Each expression represents the total number of dots in a pattern where <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>n</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> represents the step number.</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00004">
          <para id="para-00021">Try again. Revisit activities 7.2.3 and 7.2.4.</para>
          <para id="para-00022">The correct answers are <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:msup><m:mi>n</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math> and <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>n</m:mi><m:mi>·</m:mi><m:mi>n</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="_2937ceb9-af8f-40b1-8969-71308b1f2a66" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00005">
          <para id="para-00023">Use the pattern below to answer the questions.</para>
          <para id="para-00024">How many blocks are in Step 4?</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00005">
          <para id="para-00025">Correct! The length is always <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>n</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>, the width is always <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>n</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>, and then <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>n</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> blocks are subtracted.</para>
          <para id="para-00026">Try again. Revisit activities 7.3.2 and 7.3.4.</para>
          <para id="para-00027">The correct answer is 32.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="_6e40b6dc-235c-482f-a9cc-eeada42e60f2" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00006">
          <para id="para-00028">How many blocks are in Step 5?</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00006">
          <para id="para-00029">Correct! The length is always <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>n</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>, the width is always <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>n</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>, and then <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>n</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> blocks are subtracted.</para>
          <para id="para-00030">Try again. Revisit activities 7.3.2 and 7.3.4.</para>
          <para id="para-00031">The correct answer is 44.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="fdbe403b-0f9a-4799-ae16-bfce47321e47" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00007">
          <para id="para-00032">How many blocks are in Step <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>n</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>?</para>
          <para id="para-00033">Multiple Choice:</para>
          <para id="para-00034"><m:math><m:mrow><m:msup><m:mi>n</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para><para id="para-00035"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>n</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>6</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para><para id="para-00036"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>n</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mi>n</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math></para><para id="para-00037"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>n</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math></para></problem>
        <solution id="sol-00007">
          <para id="para-00038">Correct! The length is always <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>n</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>, the width is <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>n</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>, and then <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>n</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> blocks are subtracted.</para>
          <para id="para-00039">Try again. Revisit activities 7.3.2 – 7.3.4.</para>
          <para id="para-00040">The correct answer is <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>n</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mi>n</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
    </section>
  </content>
</document>